  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Multiplying Binomials</title>
      <para>Write an expression equivalent to \((x + 2)(x + 5)\).</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute. Use FOIL. Multiply the First terms, Outer terms, Inner terms, and Last terms.</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING X PLUS 2 TIMES X PLUS 5. ON THE TOP, IN RED, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO 5. ON THE BOTTOM, IN BLUE, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 2 TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 2 TO 5.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_08_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Write out the four terms.
  \(x^2+5x+2x+10\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms.
  \(x^2+7x+10\)</para>
      <note class="try look-at-me"/>
  <title>Try It: Multiplying Binomials</title>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Write an expression equivalent to \((x + 7)(x + 3)\).</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Here is how to multiply binomial expressions:</para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING X PLUS 7 TIMES X PLUS 3. ON THE TOP, IN RED, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO 3. ON THE BOTTOM, IN BLUE, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 7 TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 7 TO 3.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_08_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Write out the four terms.
    \(x^2+3x+7x+10\)</para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms.
    \(x^2+10x+21\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
</content>
